WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.003
♪♪

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:05.204
-Ladies and gentlemen,

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:07.907
please welcome Will Ferrell
and Chad Smith!

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.009
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:19.185
♪♪

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:28.327
♪♪

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:32.032
[ Cheering, applause continue ]

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:45.844
Chad, uh, Will...

00:00:45.844 --> 00:00:48.715
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:55.221
I-I heard...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.323
I know that you guys
kind of look alike.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.658
I did not know that you --
you dress similar --

00:00:59.658 --> 00:01:02.495
[ Laughter ]
...you dress alike as well.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:07.299
Uh, I'm honored to be hosting
this, uh --

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:11.671
hopefully, uh, this --
this end to this epic battle.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:14.507
I mean, you guys were upset,
and I just...

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.009
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:18.278
You're almost too angry to talk,
and I understand.

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:22.849
Um, can I just set the sta--
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.183
Can I just set the stage --

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:28.154
[ Laughter,
cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.556
I want to set the stage.
Chad, I know --

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:32.926
Chad, I can feel the heat
coming off of your bodies,

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.527
the anger and the...
-Uh-huh. Right.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.462
-...the pent-up rage
and confusion.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.832
-Yeah.
-Uh, but...

00:01:39.798 --> 00:01:41.567
-He's an impostor.
-All right.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:44.370
Chad, let's not --
Let's not start off like this.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.073
I mean, this is --
Here's what happened.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:49.141
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.141 --> 00:01:52.011
-Wait. Who are you talking to,
Will or Chad?

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:53.679
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:55.348
I'm talking to Will.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:58.083
-Yeah.
-Now, Will...

00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:00.186
-Yeah?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.624
-...this whole thing started --
You were on a Reddit AMA --

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.692
uh, February 4th.

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:08.994
Someone mentioned
that you look like Chad Smith

00:02:08.994 --> 00:02:10.997
from The Red Hot Chili Peppers.
-I had heard that.

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.031
-Yeah.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:15.802
And you responded by saying,
uh...

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:18.938
You said, "No.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.673
I am Chad Smith."

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:23.543
-That is true.
You are --

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:27.013
-And it's not true, 'cause...
he's not me.

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:29.315
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.951
-But you said that you --
it's a character that you --

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:34.120
that Will Ferrell created
called Chad Smith.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.388
-Correct.
-Yeah.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:38.424
-And I was -- I was so pissed.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:39.758
-What did you do?

00:02:39.758 --> 00:02:41.194
Do you remember where you were
when you heard that news?

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.628
-Yeah.
I was jammin'.

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:45.331
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.303
-You were jammin' --
-I was jammin' with the --

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:52.938
with the Chili Peppers,
with my guys.

00:02:52.938 --> 00:02:55.307
Yeah. In our --
At our jam house.

00:02:55.307 --> 00:02:57.476
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.476 --> 00:02:59.946
You have -- How many jam houses
do you guys have?

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.114
-In America?

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:03.615
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:03:03.615 --> 00:03:05.651
-In -- Yeah.
In America.

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:06.785
-Four.
-You have four.

00:03:06.785 --> 00:03:09.121
So this --
You're at jam house number...

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:10.957
-Three.
-...three, and you're --

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.126
And you see this thing online.

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:15.595
-I go through the roof.
-Yeah. You just went...

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:18.864
-I'm like, "Flea, this is..."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.864 --> 00:03:20.199
-You talked to Flea first.

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:22.201
-Yeah.
I go, "Flea, this is bull.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:24.536
I'm tired of this."
-You're tired of this crap.

00:03:24.536 --> 00:03:25.704
-I'm tired of being --

00:03:25.704 --> 00:03:28.207
not getting enough respect
as Chad Smith.

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:29.842
-He seems like he's
a little angry, but yeah.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:30.976
-Chad...

00:03:30.976 --> 00:03:32.812
-I'll be honest.
I'm a little high right now.

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:35.315
-All right. No, no.
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:39.385
Chad, we'll bleep all this out.

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:43.223
Uh...Chad, when did you --

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:45.291
-My Chad Smith Go Juice
right here.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.626
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:51.030
-What is in the Chad --
the Chad Smith Go Juice?

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.365
What's that made of?
Can you tell?

00:03:53.365 --> 00:03:55.367
-It's a chemical compound,

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:58.604
uh, that we make up
at the jam house -- number two.

00:03:58.604 --> 00:03:59.605
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.605 --> 00:04:00.939
-The chemical compound.

00:04:00.939 --> 00:04:03.109
-Yeah.
-All right. Understood.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:05.110
Chad, how long
have you been playing drums?

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:08.614
-I've been playing since I was,
uh...since I was 8.

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:09.782
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.117
-You remember where you were?
-Yeah.

00:04:12.117 --> 00:04:14.654
In my house.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:15.821
-What room?

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:17.156
-Uh, in -- in my bedroom.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.958
-You were in the bedroom.
You had a drum set there?

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:20.559
-Little, uh, Kmart drum set.
-Aw.

00:04:20.559 --> 00:04:23.229
You just started jammin' out?
-Yeah, I just started jammin'.

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:25.064
I knew I had a gift.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:27.566
-Yeah.
I mean, most likely, you know...

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:29.068
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.469
Yeah.

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:32.438
And, Will, how long have you
been playing the drums?

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:34.607
-I do not play the drums.
-Okay. Now...

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.576
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:41.280
-Chad, what do the bandmates
think about this?

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.648
What does...

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:44.650
-Uh, you know,
they want me to, you know,

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:45.985
tear this guy a new one,

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.120
and, uh, they're like,
"Enough is enough."

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.988
It's affecting our shows.

00:04:49.988 --> 00:04:53.159
Uh, it's affecting
the camaraderie in the band.

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:54.427
-Why?

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:56.663
-They said, "We're starting
to get brainwashed.

00:04:56.663 --> 00:04:59.364
We look back. We think that's
Will Ferrell playing drums."

00:04:59.364 --> 00:05:00.799
-The band actually thinks

00:05:00.799 --> 00:05:02.301
they're playing
with Will Ferrell.

00:05:02.301 --> 00:05:04.069
-Exactly.
-[ Sighs ] It's ridiculous.

00:05:04.069 --> 00:05:06.071
-Will, this is
the weirdest thing.

00:05:06.071 --> 00:05:09.375
But you're raising money
for charity with this drum-off.

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:13.546
Will, your charity
is CancerForCollege.org.

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:14.680
-Yes.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:18.084
-And, Chad,
yours is LittleKidsRock.org.

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:19.418
-Yeah.

00:05:19.418 --> 00:05:22.422
-So at least there's some, uh,
light at the end of this.

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:24.690
-We take instruments away
from children.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.160
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.994
-Well, how is that a good --

00:05:28.994 --> 00:05:31.464
-We take them to a-a junkyard,

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:33.799
and we destroy them
in front of the children.

00:05:33.799 --> 00:05:35.634
-And just show -- Really?
What...

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.236
-No.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:39.071
-He doesn't know
what he's talking --

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:41.073
That can't be
what that is raising money for.

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:43.242
Little Kids R-- I think
you're giving instruments --

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:46.411
-It's my charity. Chad Smith.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.411 --> 00:05:48.614
-Chad, you're, like, coming off
as a mean dude, man.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.215
I thought it was
a different charity

00:05:50.215 --> 00:05:52.217
where you actually
give instruments to schools.

00:05:52.217 --> 00:05:54.286
-It started out that way.

00:05:54.286 --> 00:05:56.656
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:02.695
But Cancer for College?
That's a great charity.

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:03.829
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:06.798
-It is.
It started with my good friend.

00:06:06.798 --> 00:06:10.369
I've had great success,
and it's a small charity,

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:14.206
but it's grassroots and it's
great that we can do this.

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:16.642
-But Little Kids Rock,
you think, is...

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:17.677
-Well, no.

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:19.011
Little Kids Rock, you know,

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:21.546
they shouldn't take instruments
from kids.

00:06:21.546 --> 00:06:23.048
-They shouldn't.
-They shouldn't...

00:06:23.048 --> 00:06:24.750
-What's wrong --
Why would you do that?

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.253
-...but we do,
and we've got a lot of support.

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:28.587
-[ Laughing ]
A lot of support.

00:06:28.587 --> 00:06:30.323
-Who's supporting that?

00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:32.858
-You'd be surprised.
-Junkyards.

00:06:32.858 --> 00:06:34.560
-Guys, enough --
enough small talk.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.962
I mean, I think you can feel
the crispiness in the air,

00:06:36.962 --> 00:06:38.464
the energy that's here.
-Yeah.

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:40.132
-You know what the audience
wants.

00:06:40.132 --> 00:06:42.335
You know what I want.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:44.103 --> 00:06:46.372
What America wants.
-Yeah.

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:48.207
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:50.442
-It's time to find out
once and for all

00:06:50.442 --> 00:06:52.712
who's the better drummer --
Will Ferrell

00:06:52.712 --> 00:06:55.882
or the drummer from The Red Hot
Chili Peppers, Chad Smith.

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:57.883
You guys ready to do this?
-We are, and --

00:06:57.883 --> 00:07:00.653
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:02.621
We were tricking you
that whole time.

00:07:02.621 --> 00:07:05.858
This is Chad Smith,
and I'm Will Ferrell, actually.

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:07.192
-You got to be kidding me.
-Yeah.

00:07:07.192 --> 00:07:09.895
So just so we know
who's really doing the drumming.

00:07:09.895 --> 00:07:11.130
-You know what that means.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.965
Let's bring out the drums
right here.

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:14.800
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Drum-off!

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:15.901
[ Drums beating ]

00:07:15.901 --> 00:07:21.173
♪♪

00:07:21.173 --> 00:07:26.445
♪♪

00:07:26.445 --> 00:07:29.615
[ Cheers and applause ]
-All right. Now just...

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:32.017
All right.
And that's Will.

00:07:32.017 --> 00:07:34.286
Okay. Very good.
Now...

00:07:34.286 --> 00:07:36.622
Oh.
Holy mackerel. Uh...

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:39.124
[ Bass drum playing,
crowd cheering ]

00:07:39.124 --> 00:07:41.293
Seem about right?

00:07:41.293 --> 00:07:42.662
-Yeah.
-Seem about right?

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:44.163
[ Laughter ]

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:46.665
All right, guys.
You know the rules.

00:07:46.665 --> 00:07:49.134
Uh, this is a traditional
drum-off.

00:07:49.134 --> 00:07:51.504
[ Laughter ]
-This is a traditional drum-off?

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:53.739
-What's that?
-This is a traditional drum-off?

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:55.775
-Tonight we're gonna go
by traditional rules.

00:07:55.775 --> 00:07:57.442
[ Laughter ]

00:07:57.442 --> 00:07:59.711
This is a traditional drum-off.

00:07:59.711 --> 00:08:02.180
You each get four solos.

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:05.985
Uh, whoever whacks, smacks, and
slaps the skins the best wins.

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:09.588
So without further ado,
let the drum-off begin!

00:08:09.588 --> 00:08:12.792
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:23.269
-Let's go, Will!

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:25.838
[ Crowd cheering ]

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:28.340
-Ladies first!

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:30.509
-Take notes, Chadwick.

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:32.678
[ Laughter ]

00:08:32.678 --> 00:08:41.220
♪♪

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:44.222
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:44.222 --> 00:08:46.826
And that's how it's done.

00:08:48.327 --> 00:08:50.462
-All right.

00:08:50.462 --> 00:08:59.305
♪♪

00:08:59.305 --> 00:09:02.707
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:02.707 --> 00:09:05.010
